  "description": "The WHEN OTHER arm at app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl:99-102, reached with PF5 - a key the program has no arm for. Line 100 sets WS-ERR-FLG to 'Y' and line 101 moves CCDA-MSG-INVALID-KEY into WS-MESSAGE: a PIC X(50) sender (app/cpy/CSMSG01Y.cpy:20) into a PIC X(80) receiver, so the fifty characters are left-justified and the remaining thirty are spaces, which is what the WS_MESSAGE_80 expectation below spells out in full. That literal is deliberately NOT CCDA-TITLE01's or CCDA-THANK-YOU's X(40) text: the two are different fields of different widths and substituting one for the other is a parity failure. PROCESS-ENTER-KEY is not performed on this arm, so OPTIONO is not rewritten and keeps the value the client re-supplied - '7 ' here, exactly as typed and NOT normalised to '07' - which is statelessness made visible: the screen field survives only because it travelled in the payload.",
